1
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:28,500
There is no defense.

2
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:51,000
The Juror is a thriller, crime, drama film directed by Brian Gibson.

3
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:13,500
With his gangster boss on trial for murder, a mob thug known as "the Teacher" tells Annie Laird she must talk her
fellow jurors into a not-guilty verdict, implying that he'll kill her son Oliver if she fails.

4
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
She manages to do this, but, when it becomes clear that the mobsters might want to silence her for good, she sends
Oliver abroad and tries to gather evidence of the plot against her, setting up a final showdown.

5
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:58,500
Annie Laird, played by Demi Moore.

6
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Teacher, played by Alec Baldwin.

7
00:51:37,500 --> 00:51:43,500
Oliver Laird, played by Joseph Gordon-Levitt.

8
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
Juliet, played by Anne Heche.

9
01:06:22,500 --> 01:06:28,500
Eddie, played by James Gandolfini.

10
01:13:45,000 --> 01:13:51,000
Tallow, played by Lindsay Crouse.

11
01:21:07,500 --> 01:21:13,500
The Juror is a 1996 American legal thriller film based
on the 1995 novel by George Dawes Green.

12
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:36,000
It was directed by Brian Gibson and stars Demi Moore as a single mother picked for jury
duty for a mafia trial and Alec Baldwin as a mobster sent to intimidate her.

13
01:35:52,500 --> 01:35:58,500
The film received highly negative reviews and Moore won a joint Golden Raspberry Award
for Worst Actress for both her performance in this film and in Striptease.

14
01:43:15,000 --> 01:43:21,000
The film explores themes of court case, jurors, blackmail, son, trial.

15
01:50:37,500 --> 01:50:43,500
The tone is emotional and intense.
